~I'm pretty sure that's normal behavior, environment variables set in the system dialog are refreshed on windows reboot only.
Does it work differently if you launch the terminal from the start menu instead of Files?~

** Edit: ah I'm afraid the new process is inheriting env variables (old) from Files. We need to read them again when starting the terminal, e.g:
```cs
psi.EnvironmentVariables.Clear();
foreach (DictionaryEntry ent in Environment.GetEnvironmentVariables(EnvironmentVariableTarget.Machine))
    psi.EnvironmentVariables[(string)ent.Key] = (string)ent.Value;
foreach (DictionaryEntry ent in Environment.GetEnvironmentVariables(EnvironmentVariableTarget.User))
    psi.EnvironmentVariables[(string)ent.Key] = (string)ent.Value;
```
